             :intent "`seon.ref/references` answers `:unresolved` for a var whose namespace is on the classpath but not loaded: `seon.operator/check!` (Babashka script) and `rewrite-clj.paredit/slurp-backward` both did on default (2026-10-08, loaded commit 32ca5f2e5), because `library-name` requires `find-ns`. clj-kondo's dependency cache, which boot fills (`seon.fn.analyzer/ensure-dependency-analysis!`), holds each var's row and arities with the file in its pinned extract; `clj-kondo.impl.cache/from-cache-1` reads one namespace in under 1 ms. Done when an unloaded name resolves from that cache with its row, arglists, first doc line (read from the form at the row with edamame) and pin, and an absent one stays unresolved; a row in `seon.ref-test` covers both names."
             :must-read #{seon.ref/references seon.fn.analyzer/ensure-dependency-analysis! clj-kondo.impl.cache/from-cache-1}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/files/files-opus.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-must-read-offers-a-source-form-that-answers-nil"
